IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ar62-nouns`

-- Row il-62. THE ONE REFERENCE, as typed values, and its control.
-- A reference to a range of paragraphs is encoded as the range the citing words name (the first paragraph and the last) and one record for each paragraph of the list: whether the consolidation prints text for it,
-- whether the consolidation prints it as deleted, and whether an official instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted. A test counts the paragraphs the range names that are deleted.
-- Where the count is not zero the range names a paragraph that is not there; that is the finding, kept in an expected-red file with its count declared in check.sh and encoding.json.
-- THE FINDING: the words that end s 35(b) cite "בפסקאות (1) עד (5)"; paragraph (5) of the list is printed by the consolidation as "(נמחקה)" and an instrument printed in Sefer HaChukim 2556 directs that it be deleted.
-- CONTROL: paragraphs (1) to (4) of the same list, each of which the consolidation prints with text and none of which any instrument read by this row directs be deleted.
-- LIMBS. Limb (a) is the question whether the target is as the citing words say it is (here: whether each paragraph the range names is there); limb (b) is the question whether the citing words still read so in the latest official text.
-- Each limb says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in ar62-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource text is not official.
-- A date for which the sources held give no answer is NOTHING; there is no REFUSE. The day on which the deletion took effect was not read, and this row types no such day.

§ `The range and the paragraphs it names`

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
      p IS A `A paragraph of the list`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the range names the paragraph` MEANS
    p's `its number` AT LEAST r's `the first paragraph named`
    AND p's `its number` AT MOST r's `the last paragraph named`

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
      p IS A `A paragraph of the list`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if the range names the paragraph and the consolidation prints it as deleted` MEANS
    IF `the range names the paragraph` r p AND p's `the consolidation prints it as deleted`
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
      p IS A `A paragraph of the list`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if the range names the paragraph and an instrument read by this row directs its deletion` MEANS
    IF `the range names the paragraph` r p AND p's `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted`
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
      p IS A `A paragraph of the list`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if the range names the paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the range names the paragraph` r p THEN 1 ELSE 0

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of paragraphs the range names` MEANS
    `one if the range names the paragraph` r (`paragraph (1) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph` r (`paragraph (2) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph` r (`paragraph (3) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph` r (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph` r (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of paragraphs the range names that the consolidation prints as deleted` MEANS
    `one if the range names the paragraph and the consolidation prints it as deleted` r (`paragraph (1) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and the consolidation prints it as deleted` r (`paragraph (2) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and the consolidation prints it as deleted` r (`paragraph (3) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and the consolidation prints it as deleted` r (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and the consolidation prints it as deleted` r (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of paragraphs the range names that an instrument read by this row directs be deleted` MEANS
    `one if the range names the paragraph and an instrument read by this row directs its deletion` r (`paragraph (1) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and an instrument read by this row directs its deletion` r (`paragraph (2) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and an instrument read by this row directs its deletion` r (`paragraph (3) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and an instrument read by this row directs its deletion` r (`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)`)
    + `one if the range names the paragraph and an instrument read by this row directs its deletion` r (`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)`)

GIVEN r IS A `A range reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every paragraph the range names is printed with text by the consolidation` MEANS
    `the number of paragraphs the range names that the consolidation prints as deleted` r EQUALS 0

§ `Printed date pairs`

GIVEN p IS A `A printed date pair`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the printed pair matches the routine` MEANS p's `the Gregorian date printed with it` EQUALS p's `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives`

-- THE CITING WORDS (limb b). The tail line of s 35(b) in the consolidation, after the list of paragraphs, with the paragraph lines it cites.
-- CONSOLIDATION-ONLY for every line below, as to what the Law prints today: the instrument of 2005 prints the words "(1) עד (5)" as a replacement in its section 51(1), and the instrument of 2016 has no instruction that names them;
-- that the tail still reads so today is read from the consolidation alone.
-- src:470 | (ב) בחוק זה, ”חשוד בעבירת בטחון“ – מי שחשוד בעבירה לפי אחד מאלה:
-- src:471 | (1) סימן ב׳ או סימן ד׳ בפרק ז׳ לחוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977, וכן סעיפים 122א, 146, 143, 144, ו־147 לחוק האמור;
-- src:472 | (2) תקנות 58, 59, 62 ו־64 לתקנות ההגנה (שעת חירום), 1945;
-- src:473 | (3) עבירת טרור חמורה כהגדרתה בחוק המאבק בטרור, התשע״ו–2016;
-- src:474 | (4) חוק למניעת הסתננות (עבירות ושיפוט), התשי״ד–1954;
-- src:475 | (5) [note: (נמחקה);]
-- src:476 | או מי שעצור לפי חוק להארכת תוקפן של תקנות שעת חירום (יהודה והשומרון וחבל עזה – שיפוט בעבירות ועזרה משפטית), התשכ״ח–1967, והוא חשוד בעבירה שאילו נעברה בישראל היתה אחת מהעבירות המנויות בפסקאות (1) עד (5).
-- THE ADDING INSTRUMENT (limb a, paragraph (5)). Sefer HaChukim 1973 (29 Tevet 5765, 10 January 2005), printed p. 89, read from the page image: section 51 amends s 35(b) of the Law and adds paragraph (5).
-- ext:[SH 1973 p.89, read from the page image] | 51. בחוק סדר הדין הפלילי (סמכויות אכיפה – מעצרים), התשנ"ו–1996, בסעיף 35(ב) –
-- ext:[SH 1973 p.89, read from the page image] | (1) בפסקה (4), במקום "(1) עד (4)" יבוא "(1) עד (5)";
-- ext:[SH 1973 p.89, read from the page image] | (2) אחרי פסקה (4) יבוא:
-- ext:[SH 1973 p.89, read from the page image] | "(5) סעיף 8 לחוק איסור מימון טרור, התשס"ה–2005."
-- ext:[SH 1973 p.89, read from the page image; text layer not checked: the page has none for the footer] | ספר החוקים 1973, כ"ט בטבת התשס"ה, 10.1.2005
-- THE DELETING INSTRUMENT (limb a, paragraph (5)). Sefer HaChukim 2556 (17 Sivan 5776, 23 June 2016), printed p. 927, read from the page image: section 86 amends s 35(b) of the Law in three items;
-- the third directs that paragraph (5) be deleted. The day on which the deletion took effect was not read, because the instrument's section on commencement is not among the pages read.
-- ext:[SH 2556 p.927, read from the page image] | 86. בחוק סדר הדין הפלילי (סמכויות אכיפה – מעצרים), התשנ"ו–1996, בסעיף 35(ב) –
-- ext:[SH 2556 p.927, read from the page image] | (1) בפסקה (2), במקום "64, 66, 67, 84 ו־85" יבוא "ו־64";
-- ext:[SH 2556 p.927, read from the page image] | (2) במקום פסקה (3) יבוא:
-- ext:[SH 2556 p.927, read from the page image] | "(3) עבירת טרור חמורה כהגדרתה בחוק המאבק בטרור, התשע"ו–2016;";
-- ext:[SH 2556 p.927, read from the page image] | (3) פסקה (5) – תימחק.
-- ext:[SH 2556 p.927, read from the page image] | ספר החוקים 2556, י"ז בסיוון התשע"ו, 23.6.2016
-- Limb (b): none of the three items of section 86 names the words "(1) עד (5)" of the tail: they edit paragraph (2), replace paragraph (3) and delete paragraph (5), and the tail is none of these.
-- That later instruments left the tail as it is today is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY; later official instruments that touch s 35 were opened and are not deposited, and this row rests on none of them.
`range: the words "(1) עד (5)" at the end of s 35(b)` MEANS
    `A range reference` WITH
        `the citing words are in` IS "Criminal Procedure (Enforcement Powers - Arrests) Law, s 35(b), the tail words 'בפסקאות (1) עד (5)'"
        `the first paragraph named` IS 1
        `the last paragraph named` IS 5
        `limb (b) was read from` IS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

-- THE PARAGRAPHS OF THE LIST. Paragraphs (1) to (4) are the CONTROL: the consolidation prints text for each (lines 471 to 474 above), and no instrument read by this row directs that any of them be deleted;
-- items (1) and (2) of section 86 edit paragraph (2) and replace paragraph (3), which is not deletion. What each of them says is not discussed here.
-- Paragraph (1): the sound paragraph beside the finding.
`paragraph (1) of s 35(b)` MEANS
    `A paragraph of the list` WITH
        `its number` IS 1
        `the consolidation prints text for it` IS TRUE
        `the consolidation prints it as deleted` IS FALSE
        `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted` IS FALSE
        `the instrument that adds it` IS "not read by this row"
        `the instrument that directs its deletion` IS "none read by this row"
        `limb (a) was read from` IS `the consolidation only`

`paragraph (2) of s 35(b)` MEANS
    `A paragraph of the list` WITH
        `its number` IS 2
        `the consolidation prints text for it` IS TRUE
        `the consolidation prints it as deleted` IS FALSE
        `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted` IS FALSE
        `the instrument that adds it` IS "not read by this row"
        `the instrument that directs its deletion` IS "none read by this row"
        `limb (a) was read from` IS `the consolidation only`

`paragraph (3) of s 35(b)` MEANS
    `A paragraph of the list` WITH
        `its number` IS 3
        `the consolidation prints text for it` IS TRUE
        `the consolidation prints it as deleted` IS FALSE
        `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted` IS FALSE
        `the instrument that adds it` IS "not read by this row"
        `the instrument that directs its deletion` IS "none read by this row"
        `limb (a) was read from` IS `the consolidation only`

-- Paragraph (4): the control named by the brief of this row, a paragraph that exists.
`paragraph (4) of s 35(b)` MEANS
    `A paragraph of the list` WITH
        `its number` IS 4
        `the consolidation prints text for it` IS TRUE
        `the consolidation prints it as deleted` IS FALSE
        `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted` IS FALSE
        `the instrument that adds it` IS "not read by this row"
        `the instrument that directs its deletion` IS "none read by this row"
        `limb (a) was read from` IS `the consolidation only`

-- Paragraph (5): the target of the finding. Added by section 51(2) of Sefer HaChukim 1973, p. 89; printed by the consolidation as deleted (line 475 above, CONSOLIDATION-ONLY);
-- directed deleted by section 86(3) of Sefer HaChukim 2556, p. 927 (read from the page image). That no later instrument restored it is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
`paragraph (5) of s 35(b)` MEANS
    `A paragraph of the list` WITH
        `its number` IS 5
        `the consolidation prints text for it` IS FALSE
        `the consolidation prints it as deleted` IS TRUE
        `an instrument read by this row directs that it be deleted` IS TRUE
        `the instrument that adds it` IS "section 51(2) of Sefer HaChukim 1973, printed p. 89"
        `the instrument that directs its deletion` IS "section 86(3) of Sefer HaChukim 2556, printed p. 927"
        `limb (a) was read from` IS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

-- THE DATE PAIRS. Each Hebrew date below was converted with the Hebrew-calendar routine in tools/hebcal.py (tools/datepairs.py runs the conversions and the routine's own control, 30 Kislev 5785 = 31 December 2024, first).
-- Each pair is on the footer line of the page named: the ext line above.
`date pair: the footer of printed p. 89 of Sefer HaChukim 1973` MEANS
    `A printed date pair` WITH
        `the Hebrew date, transliterated` IS "29 Tevet 5765"
        `the Gregorian date printed with it` IS Date 10 1 2005
        `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives` IS Date 10 1 2005
        `the pair was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

`date pair: the footer of printed p. 927 of Sefer HaChukim 2556` MEANS
    `A printed date pair` WITH
        `the Hebrew date, transliterated` IS "17 Sivan 5776"
        `the Gregorian date printed with it` IS Date 23 6 2016
        `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives` IS Date 23 6 2016
        `the pair was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
